<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philistines</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th–7th centuries BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Philistines were a people who settled the southern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canaan">Canaan</a> in the twelfth century BCE, probably among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-peoples">Sea Peoples</a>, with material culture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> origin. They formed a league of five cities, the Philistine Pentapolis of Gaza, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashkelon">Ashkelon</a>, Ashdod, Ekron and Gath. Known in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a> as enemies of Israel, they lost their independence to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philistines.jpg" alt="Philistines" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ant888nsmb2 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sea_people02_upscayl_1x_remacri-4x.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
